### Why is identifying the critical path important for project managers?
Knowing the critical path allows project managers to monitor progress effectively and take corrective actions early when delays occur.

### Which activity posed the highest scheduling risk?
Testing and Validation posed the highest scheduling risk because bugs or performance issues can require repeated fixes and retesting.

### What trade-offs are involved when crashing a project?
Shortening task durations may increase expenses and stress on team members, and it can introduce risks if tasks are rushed.
